@node PART_01 "Introduction"

For sysops it's hard to keep their conferences up to date. This door
checks if the files stated in the catalogs still exist. If they don't
exists anymore, the filesize in the catalog will be changed to a text
like 'OFFLINE', 'DELETED' or something simular.

The door is very smart, so the less installation you have to do. It
checks the following icons BBS:CONFCONFIG and CONF<num>. Lets enjoy
this one.

@endnode

@node PART_02 "Requirements"

What U need to run it...
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

 - an Amigamodel (A500/A600/A1200/A2000/A3000/A4000) with Kickstart 2.04++

 - the installed /X-Software (V3.20+) in the drawer BBS:

Now let's go on by explaining the @{"Installation" LINK PART_03}...

@endnode

@node PART_03 "Installation for ConfUpdater 1.9"

How to install it to your /X-System...
~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

First make a Drawer into Doors: called 'MDB-ConfUpdater' and copy the Files
 - 'MDB-ConfUpdater'
 - 'MDB-ConfUpdater.INFO'
into it.

Second copy the Icon 'CU.INFO' into the BBSCmd Drawer.

Last bu not least you have to copy some tools into the C Drawer, coz
the insert-option need them to extract the FILE_ID.DIZ. These files are:
 - 'DMSDescript'
 - 'EXEDescript'
 - 'TxtExtract'

Thats all there is. Simple he!

@endnode

@node PART_04 "ToolTypes for ConfUpdater 1.9"

                                ToolTypes
                                ~~~~~~~~~

                    @{" TOOLTYPES FOR MDB-ConfUpdater 1.9" LINK PART_04_LC}

                    @{" TOOLTYPES FOR CU                 " LINK PART_04_LO}

@endnode

@node PART_04_LC "ToolTypes for MDB-ConfUpdater 1.9

                 ToolTypes for MDB-ConfUpdater 1.9
                 ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

DELETE.num=<string>             - The DELETE.num tooltype specifies the text
                                  that will be passed to your catalogs. The
                                  maximum string length is 8 characters. Do
                                  not overide this one. The maximum of
                                  DELETE.num is 9.
                                  Eg. DELETE.1=OFFLINE

DESTINATION=<path>              - This tooltype specifies where the DIR<num>
                                  catalogs will be stored. It is a backup-
                                  mechanism, so you have to move them your
                                  self to active them. The catalogs will be
                                  be stored as CONF<num>_DIR<num>. The path
                                  must end with a ':' or a '/' like:
                                  DESTINATION=RAM: or
                                  DESTINATION=Work:Tmp/
@endnode

@node PART_04_LO "ToolTypes For CU"

                       ToolTypes for CU
                       ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~

ACCESS=<acs.level>              - This tooltype specifies the access level
                                  that the user must have to run the door.
                                  Eg. ACCESS=200

LOCATION=<filename>             - This tooltype specifies where the Door
                                  is located.
                                  LOCATION=Doors:MDB-ConfUpdater/MDB-ConfUpdater
                                  !!! DO NOT CHANGE THIS ONE !!!

MULTINODE=<YES|NO>              - This tooltype specifies if the Door may
                                  started in different nodes.
                                  Eg. MULTINODE=YES

PRIORITY=<num>                  - This tooltype specifies the AmigaDos
                                  priority when the Door is executed.
                                  Eg. PRIORITY=2

STACK=<size>                    - This tooltype specifies the Door stack.
                                  Eg. STACK=8096

TYPE=<AIM|SIM|TIM|XIM>          - This tooltype specifies the Door-type.
                                  This Door is written in 100% pure
                                  Assembly so TYPE=XIM

@endnode

@node PART_05 "Commands"

Start the door by useing the CU-command, and will get the main menu.

@{" A "} Shows some litte information about the authors.

@{" D "} In a conference you can use different DIRs. The maximum is
    stated in the CONF<num> icon in the tooltype NDIRS. By 
    startup this value will be used as working DIR. This option
    allows you to change the dirnumber you are working with.

@{" U "} THE CONFERENCE UPDATE. This one scans your current dir (as
    mentions with option D). If a entry in your dir doesn't
    exists anymore, a action will take place:
       1. change the filesize in a message like 'DELETED'
       2. delete the entry.
    Which one will depant of your option (1-0).

@{" Q "} Don't try.

@{" I "} This one scans all your update dirs. If there is a file 
    which is not present in the current dir, the file will
    be added to this dir.

@{" V "} A previously processed dir can be viewed with this option.

@{" B "} We always say, safety first. Therefore an updated dir is
    placed in a directory according the DESTINATION tooltype.
    But if you want, you can the bring the processed dir only.
    Safety first, so a backup will be made of your actual dir
    in the bbs.

@{" S "} Sorts the dir by date, filename.

@endnode

@node PART_06 "Changes"

1.9 (05 Jun May 1994)
    - The dir can now be sorted! It's even possible to make all
      files with current date; nice for the 'N S U' command.
      Be aware for look a likes, I just saw one from noCtyre/Mystic!!!
    - Dir viewer works remote now!

1.8 (02 Jun May 1994)
    - All functions recognise the Exorcist commands! Nice he!
      Thanxs to RubiX from TFA for mentioning.

1.7 (02 Jun May 1994)
    - Viewer changed, now it uses de DT_LINELENGTH function and
      correctly displays the text options in stead of the filesize
      (the last char wasn't displayed).

1.6 (29 May 1994)
    - Some maincoding changes, faster and better!
    - The DIRs will be re-read after each DLPATH is scanned by
      the Insert-option. No duplicate entries any more!
    - Now the door uses the online BBS dir by the Insert-option
      if you answer is NO to the question if you like to use the
      previously processed dir.
    - Handles empty dirs (0 bytes or doesn't exist) correcty by
      the Insert-option.

1.5 (20 May 1994)
    - Scans download directories 1 to 9 and insert new files to
      the DIR.
    - View the processed dir.
    - Brings the processed dir online.
    - Default startup for directory changed from DIR1 to NDIRS as
      stated in CONF<num>.INFO
    - Delete an entry in the dir if the file doesn't exists.
    - A lot more, I already forgot them.

1.4 (16 May 1994) Never released
    
1.3 (16 Mar 1994)
    - Faster screenhandling.
    - New action available, directory occurences will be deleted when
      the file is not available.

1.2 (14 Mar 1994)
    - Returncode $a removed. This value meant LINE DOWN in stead
      of NEW LINE in ANSI-codes.

1.1 (13 Mar 1994) 
    - The term 'catalog' changed to 'dir' for better understanding
      for some persons.
    - Using ANSI-codes instead of CSI-codes. The screens must work
      remote now!

@endnode

